<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ's National Bank shows strong first quarter.</title>
<headline>NZ's National Bank shows strong first quarter.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of New Zealand said on Monday it had posted a 30 percent rise in pre-tax operating surplus in the March quarter, to NZ$52 million.</p>
<p>The result compares to a $40 million surplus for the three months ended March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Total income was $153 million, up 8.5 percent on the year-ago quarter result of $141 million.</p>
<p>The National Bank of New Zealand is owned by Lloyds TSB of London.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
